  "id": "primary-visual-system",
  "term": "primary visual system",
  "definition": "The primary visual system is the part of vision responsible for ordinary seeing functions such as forming images and detecting motion. In this source, it is contrasted with the circadian visual system because its development shows experience-dependent plasticity and is more affected by monocular light deprivation.",
